===Etymology 1===
{{unknown|en|Origin unknown}}; a number of possibilities have been suggested:<ref name="WD">{{cite-web|title=Fugazy Redux: Looking for the Real Fake|url=http://www.word-detective.com/2008/02/fugazy-redux/|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20170708022831/http://www.word-detective.com/2008/02/fugazy-redux/|archivedate=8 July 2017|work=The Word Detective|date=12 February 2008}}.</ref>

* A corruption of {{cog|fr|fougasse|t=type of land mine}}; [[w:Flame fougasse|flame fougasses]] were used extensively in the [[w:Korean War|Korean]] and [[w:Vietnam War|Vietnam Wars]].
* A {{glossary|backronym}} of “fucked up, got ambushed, zipped in [a body bag]” (compare {{m|en|FUBAR}}).
* Less plausibly, from [[w:English language|English]] {{m|en|fugacious|t=fleeting}} or cognates such as {{cog|it|fugace|t=fleeting}}.

